<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Central and Southern Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Nosy Be</h1><p class="st-meta">1841 CE – 1896 CE · capital Hell-Ville</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">An island off northwest Madagascar placed under French protection in 1841, an early base for France's later conquest of Madagascar.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sakalava">Sakalava</a> rulers of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/boina">Boina</a>, retreating before the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/merina-kingdom">Merina Kingdom</a>, took refuge on Nosy Be and neighbouring islands. Their queen, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsiomeko">Tsiomeko</a>, sought French protection, and in 1841 the island was ceded to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> through Admiral de Hell, governor of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ile-bourbon">Bourbon</a>, after whom its main town, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hell-ville">Hell-Ville</a>, was named.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>French administrators developed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a> cane plantations, using Malagasy, Comoran and later contract labourers, and the island became a trading centre for northwest <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a>. It was governed as a small dependency, at times jointly with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/colony-of-mayotte-and-dependencies">Mayotte</a>, and offered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> a strategic claim to the Malagasy coast.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madagascar">Madagascar</a>, Nosy Be was merged in 1896 into the new colony of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-madagascar">French Madagascar</a>. It later became known for ylang-ylang essential oil, vanilla and tourism.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="colony, 1841 CE – 1896 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 64 H80 L70 78 H30 Z"/><path d="M50 64 V18"/><path d="M50 22 L72 56 H50"/><path d="M50 28 L32 56 H50"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">colony</p><p class="st-emblem-region